## 🎯 **MVP Definition (v0.0.1 - The Real One)**

**Goal:** Automate intake → discovery → template generation → data validation. Human handles everything after that.

**NOT included:** Mapping automation, dry-run import, production import, support, training, infra provisioning.

---

## 📦 **PART 1: Frontend (Next.js)**

### **1.1 Pages You Need**

```
/                          → Landing page (simple pitch)
/intake                    → Multi-step intake form
/dashboard/:projectId      → Project dashboard
/projects                  → List all projects
/upload/:projectId         → File upload page
/validation/:projectId     → Validation results page

```

### **1.2 Components You Need**

**Intake Form:**

- Company details (name, industry, size, location)
- Current systems (Excel, legacy software, nothing)
- Pain points (multi-select checkboxes)
- Modules needed (Manufacturing, Inventory, Sales, etc.)
- Timeline & budget
- Contact info
- Submit button → creates project

**Dashboard:**

- Project status (Created → Discovery → Templates Ready → Uploaded → Validated)
- Progress bar
- Discovery results (ERP recommendation, confidence score, reasoning)
- Download templates button
- Upload data section
- Validation results section

**Upload Interface:**

- Drag-drop CSV upload
- File list with status
- Upload progress
- Error messages

**Validation Results:**

- Summary (X errors, Y warnings, Z records)
- Detailed error list (row-by-row)
- Download error report CSV
- "Request Review" button (emails you)

### **1.3 Auth (Keep Simple)**

- Email/password (use Supabase Auth or NextAuth)
- One user = one company
- No complex RBAC yet

---

## 🔧 **PART 2: Backend (FastAPI)**

### **2.1 API Endpoints**

```python
POST   /api/intake              # Submit intake form
GET    /api/projects            # List all projects
GET    /api/projects/:id        # Get project details
POST   /api/projects/:id/upload # Upload CSV files
GET    /api/projects/:id/validation # Get validation results
POST   /api/projects/:id/request-review # Notify you manually
GET    /api/templates/:projectId # Download templates

```

### **2.2 Core Services**

**Intake Service:**

- Validate input
- Sanitize data (remove PII before logging)
- Create project in DB
- Trigger discovery workflow
- Return project_id

**Discovery Service:**

- Fetch similar past projects (vector search)
- Build prompt with context
- Call LLM (GPT-4)
- Parse structured output
- Store recommendation
- Emit event

**Template Service:**

- Load ERPNext schemas
- Generate CSV templates based on selected modules
- Store in S3/storage
- Return download URLs

**Upload Service:**

- Receive files
- Validate file type/size
- Store in S3/storage
- Create upload record
- Trigger validation

**Validation Service:**

- Load CSV
- Check schema (columns match template)
- Check data types
- Check required fields
- Check duplicates
- Detect anomalies
- Generate report
- Store results

